Track 3: Flutter-Loss on the Swarm Meridian
- Story & Context: When scrap salvagers broke into the Vane-Moreau wintering grounds along the frozen Elbe river basin years after the troupe vanished, they discovered all nine caravan trucks parked in a defensive circle under a heavy shroud of black locomotive soot. Inside the master trailer sat an automated mechanical drum engine running on residual generator fumes, autonomously striking a pair of drilled brass hi-hats that had beaten uninterrupted until the alloy wore paper-thin. A looping quarter-inch master tape had caught the last room-resonance of the vanished wedding party, endlessly replaying a terrifying, ghost-choir cadence that echoed through the valley: "No wings survive the iron freeze." The recording stands as the genre's mythic epilogue, played annually through PA horns at the close of every underground Molter gathering before the power lines are cut.
